his paper name side out.

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:33.680
- Oh he's good.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.730
- And I have Scully which
means Captain Holt has me,

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:38.593
I'll be taking that gift
card, daddy loves nachos.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.790
- Shall we draw the names
again and leave Jake out?

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:43.990
- [All] Yeah.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.490
- No Sherlock wants a present.

00:09:47.470 --> 00:09:48.303
- Thank you Margaret.

00:09:48.303 --> 00:09:49.490
- You're welcome Raymond.

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:52.280
- Seamus Murphy.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.570
- That's right.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.460
Remember how I saved your
detectives from prison

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.785
in exchange for a favor?

00:09:56.785 --> 00:09:58.100
The time has come--

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.460
- Wait this isn't my order.

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:00.293
- What?

00:10:00.293 --> 00:10:02.000
- This isn't my omelet, I
only eat omelets on vacation.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.000
- Yeah, I don't care what you eat,

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.300
I'm here to call in the
favor that you owe me.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.863
- Really, what if I say no?

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.980
- This is you asking me
for intel and promising

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.790
to pay me back, how do
you think this would look

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.270
to your bosses, especially
now that you're up

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.583
for the Commissioner job?

00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:19.260
Yeah, I know everything.

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.053
- So, what do you want from me?

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.990
- A permit to throw a block party?

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.960
We don't even have to break the
law, this is fantastic news.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:30.880
- I am not giving Seamus
Murphy that permit.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.310
He only wants to use the block party

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.630
as a cover for something criminal.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.960
A robbery, a murder, or something worse.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:38.070
- You don't know that for
sure, and that's your loophole.

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.030
- I don't believe in loopholes.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:39.863
- What?

00:10:39.863 --> 00:10:40.900
Loopholes are the best, remember that time

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.730
when Pancake Palace had
that all you can eat deal

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:44.000
but they didn't set a time limit.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.810
I ate pancakes for a week for 3.99.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:48.950
All I had to do was sleep
there and never shower.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:49.783
- What?

00:10:49.783 --> 00:10:50.950
Thanks for the invite friend.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.750
- I will not be using a loophole Peralta.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.219
As always I'll be using
the main hole or no hole,

00:10:55.219 --> 00:10:56.447
I choose no hole.

00:10:56.447 --> 00:10:58.350
- You just said hole way too much sir.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:00.050
- And that's coming from Charles.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.410
- Yes, that's concerning.

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.160
- Oh you think you know
someone Jake, unbelievable.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.150
- Accounts of the first
Punic war in the year 263--

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:11.060
- Ah yes the first pubic
war, the sexiest of all wars.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.480
Hi Dr. Alberin Einstive, I've
an urgent question for you

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.680
about Ancient Greece, shall we walk?

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.060
- Of course, Dr, I feel
like you said Einstive?

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.550
- Yes that's correct, it's a family name.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.410
- What is going on?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.860
- Captain Holt sent me,
just follow my lead.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:24.710
Your theory is wrong, the Greeks did not

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.470
climb out of the Trojan horses butt.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.330
- Put this on.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:28.510
- A rose shearing hat at work,

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.192
people will think I'm demented.

00:11:30.192 --> 00:11:31.197
- Just put it on.

00:11:31.197 --> 00:11:32.030
- Kevin, Dr Einstive.

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:32.863
- Ah Professor McGonagall.

00:11:32.863 --> 00:11:34.245
- Why is Boyle dressed as me?

00:11:34.245 --> 00:11:35.246
- Shh.

00:11:35.246 --> 00:11:36.079
Get in.

00:11:36.079 --> 00:11:37.653
- But this cart is--
- Get in.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.053
Professor.
- Student.

00:11:45.622 --> 00:11:48.372
(dramatic music)

00:12:00.259 --> 00:12:01.780
- Hello Kevin, it's me Raymond Holt.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:04.000
We need to get you to safety,
your life is in danger.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.310
- Peralta there was a boss
B&amp;E at a jewelry store

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:08.468
in Atlanta that just turned
into a hostage situation,

00:12:08.468 --> 00:12:10.390
they want you to be the negotiator.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.750
- Oh my God, my prayers
have finally been answered.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.200
- You prayed for a hostage situation?

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.340
- Yes I did, every single day.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:17.270
- I don't understand, why
isn't ESU handling this?

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.800
- Apparently the hostage
taker asked for Jake by name.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.890
- Oh yes, it's getting even cooler.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:22.830
Oh man I wonder who it is?

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:25.130
Ooh, maybe it's the brother of
someone I put away for life.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:27.278
Ooh, or the identical twin of
someone I put away for life.

00:12:27.278 --> 00:12:28.710
Ooh, or the fraternal twin of--

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.423
- Jake, just get down there,
and take Diaz with you.

00:12:30.423 --> 00:12:31.950
- Yep, yep, yep, yep, how do I look?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:33.765
It doesn't matter, let's go negotiate.

00:12:33.765 --> 00:12:36.400
(sirens wailing)

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:39.380
Hey everyone, I'm here, I'm Jake Peralta,

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.310
the negotiator.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.760
- Oh so you're Jake Peralta.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:42.950
- The negotiator, yes.

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:43.783
Who are you?

00:12:43.783 --> 00:12:46.350
- Dennis Cole, ESU,
this was my crime scene

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:47.625
before you bozos got here.

00:12:47.625 --> 00:12:48.900
- Nice to meet you too Dennis.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:50.513
- I've spent 10 years as a negotiator

00:12:50.513 --> 00:12:53.300
and you just took my
first hostage situation.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:55.840
All I've done up 'til now is
talk jumpers off of rooftops.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.890
- But that must be satisfying
in it's own way right?

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:01.350
- Yeah, really satisfying
saving a crazy persons life.

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:03.090
Whatever, here's a little advice,

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:03.923
I don't like you two.

00:13:03.923 --> 00:13:05.920
- Not so much advice as
it is a hurtful statement

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:07.086
based on limited interaction.

00:13:07.086 --> 00:13:08.683
- He wants to talk to you.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:11.060
Get the hell in there.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.683
- Ooh, it says negotiator on it.

00:13:16.197 --> 00:13:18.350
This is Jake Peralta, I am unarmed,

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:21.770
and I'm approaching the building.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:32.950
You wanted to talk to me.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.900
- Keep those hands in the air.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.830
Now wave them like you just don't care.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.010
- What?

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.235
- I'm just messing with ya Peralta,

00:13:39.235 --> 00:13:41.370
put your hands down, give me a hug baby.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.321
- Judy!

00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:44.821
(tense music)

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:01.583
Oh yeah.

00:14:05.913 --> 00:14:06.910
(tapping on desk)

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:08.760
- I'm Philip Davidson,
Detective Jake Peralta

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:09.973
asked me to drop by.

00:14:09.973 --> 00:14:12.610
- Hmm, the dentist who murdered someone.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.875
Spoiler alert, they think you did it.

00:14:14.875 --> 00:14:18.240
Can you show him to
interrogation room C please.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.340
Have fun in there.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.173
- Thank you.

00:14:25.325 --> 00:14:26.158
- What are you smiling about?

00:14:26.158 --> 00:14:27.320
- How uncomfortable this guy is?

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:30.260
Jacked up the thermostat,
got the table all sticky,

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.820
made one of the chair legs too short,

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.457
and worst of all, I had Gina greet him.

00:14:33.457 --> 00:14:34.940
- What did you have her do?

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:35.950
- Be herself.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:36.940
- Poor son of a bitch.

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.570
- Yeah, why are you wearing a tuxedo?

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:40.217
- Kevin and I are attending the opera.

00:14:40.217 --> 00:14:42.451
- Ooh, the opera, is it
the one Bugs Bunny sings?

00:14:42.451 --> 00:14:45.800
- Yes, so who's this?

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.410
- This is Philip Davidson.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:48.243
- What do we have on him?

00:14:48.243 --> 00:14:49.300
- Clear motive, clear means,

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:52.150
and a non-existent alibi but
the DA won't bring a charge

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:53.524
because he says it's all circumstantial.

00:14:53.524 --> 00:14:55.530
If we wanna bring this guy
down we have to get him

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:58.130
to confess right here, right now.

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:00.570
- Hmm, an interrogation
with a ticking clock,

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:02.011
and everything on the line.

00:15:02.011 --> 00:15:04.440
I better call Kevin
and tell him I won't be

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:06.140
attending the opera, there's someone else

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:07.080
I'd rather hear sing.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.053
- Oh damn!

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:10.320
- Hello Kevin, I won't be joining you

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.317
at the opera tonight
- I'm sorry I didn't know

00:15:11.317 --> 00:15:12.150
you were on the phone already.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:12.983
- The tickets are under
- Oh damn

00:15:12.983 --> 00:15:13.816
- My name, H-O--

00:15:13.816 --> 00:15:15.700
Santiago, your test results
on the sergeants exam

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.533
has arrived.

00:15:16.533 --> 00:15:19.530
- Ooh, everybody make room,
Amy needs adequate space

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:21.010
to do her signature dork dance.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:22.425
- I don't know if there's
gonna be a dork dance.

00:15:22.425 --> 00:15:23.701
Look how small that envelope is.

00:15:23.701 --> 00:15:25.530
That's not a big good news envelope,

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.160
that's a little bad news envelope.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:28.230
- What, that's nuts.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:30.190
Serge, tell her envelope
size doesn't matter.

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:32.470
- If I'm being honest I
got a much bigger envelope.

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:33.303
- Oh God.

00:15:33.303 --> 00:15:34.280
- Unhelpful Terry, very unhelpful.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.113
- Mine was bigger too.

00:15:35.113 --> 00:15:36.910
- Okay, I just won't ever open it,

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:38.270
that way I'll never get rejected.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:39.490
- Fine, I'll open it.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.437
- No!

00:15:40.437 --> 00:15:41.484
(Jake groans)

00:15:41.484 --> 00:15:42.317
- Do it harder.

00:15:42.317 --> 00:15:43.780
- I opened it.

00:15:43.780 --> 00:15:45.170
You passed!

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:47.160
- Oh my God, I'm gonna be a sergeant.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.457
- You're gonna be a sergeant.

00:15:48.457 --> 00:15:50.042
(all cheering)

00:15:50.042 --> 00:15:52.033
- Oh no it's happening.

00:15:52.033 --> 00:15:52.866
Woo!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.543
- That's my future wife.

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.580
Pigeons still here?

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.420
- Yeah, no matter what we
do he just won't leave.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.300
- The problem is you're
thinking like detectives.

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:05.133
- No I'm definitely not.

00:16:05.133 --> 00:16:08.080
- When you should be thinking like a bird.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:11.090
This is Operation Saving Private Pigeon.

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.090
On my mark I will turn on this fan,

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.350
gently startling our bird due east

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.690
into the file box canyon
where he will encounter

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.540
Charles holding two pot lids.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.850
He'll bang them together,
forcing Private Pigeon

00:16:21.850 --> 00:16:24.510
into the ceiling there, and
out of the ceiling there,

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:26.550
where he will be greeted by scary Rosa,

00:16:26.550 --> 00:16:28.230
holding a scary picture of an owl.

00:16:28.230 --> 00:16:29.810
Now he's playing our game.

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:32.130
He'll veer left into an
upside down garbage can,

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:33.260
propped up by a hockey stick

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.070
and connected to a string
that Gina is holding.

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:38.108
She pulls it, he's trapped,
and Terry releases him outside.

00:16:38.108 --> 00:16:39.400
- Terry hates birds.

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:42.750
- Okay little friend, let's
get you home to momma.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:44.529
(fan whirring)
(Jake screams)

00:16:44.529 --> 00:16:48.500
Oh God, it flew right into
the fan, it's everywhere.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.320
There's pigeon everywhere!

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.210
So, do you recognize any of these men?

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:53.670
- I was hiding in the bathroom stall

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.500
so I didn't see his face but I heard him.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:58.390
He was singing along to
the music at the bar.

00:16:58.390 --> 00:16:59.340
- Do you remember what he was singing?

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:01.870
- I think it was that
song, "I want it that way."

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.360
- Backstreet Boys, I'm familiar.

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:04.620
Okay.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.370
Number one could you
please sing the opening

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.520
to "I want it that way."

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:08.574
- Really?

00:17:08.574 --> 00:17:10.063
Okay.

00:17:11.825 --> 00:17:14.742
♪ You are, my fire ♪

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:18.398
- Number two, keep it going.

00:17:18.398 --> 00:17:21.148
♪ The one desire ♪

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:23.543
- Number three.

00:17:23.543 --> 00:17:27.120
♪ Believe when I say ♪

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.210
- Number four.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.750
♪ I want it that way ♪

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.105
♪ Tell me why ♪

00:17:33.105 --> 00:17:36.641
♪ Aint nothing but a heartache ♪

00:17:36.641 --> 00:17:38.094
♪ Tell me why ♪

00:17:38.094 --> 00:17:41.557
♪ Aint nothing but a mistake ♪

00:17:41.557 --> 00:17:42.939
♪ Now number five ♪

00:17:42.939 --> 00:17:47.240
♪ I never wanna hear you say ♪

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.323
♪ I want it that way ♪

00:17:51.660 --> 00:17:53.790
- Oh chills, literal chills.

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.320
- It was number five, number
five killed my brother.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.060
- Oh my God, I forgot about that part.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.867
- Charles, wanna grab a
beer before you go home?

00:17:59.867 --> 00:18:01.190
- Oh a yeast feast.

00:18:01.190 --> 00:18:02.023
- Never mind.

00:18:02.023 --> 00:18:03.330
- No, no, no, I wanna go
it's just there's a huge

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:04.607
emergency I have to deal with first.

00:18:04.607 --> 00:18:05.910
- Oh no, is everything okay?

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:06.879
- It's about my food truck,

00:18:06.879 --> 00:18:08.432
I have to get a parking spot.

00:18:08.432 --> 00:18:10.020
- That doesn't sound as intense

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.260
as you were making it out to be.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:12.798
- Move your arse you old bitch.

00:18:12.798 --> 00:18:13.795
- What is happening?

00:18:13.795 --> 00:18:15.030
- We have to get there by seven o'clock

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.373
when they lift the parking restrictions.

00:18:16.373 --> 00:18:19.319
It's the best spot in Brooklyn
and everyone wants it.

00:18:19.319 --> 00:18:20.889
- Get the hell out of the way.

00:18:20.889 --> 00:18:23.470
(car horn blaring)

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:26.750
- Charles, I highly doubt the
entire food truck industry

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.480
is racing to get into this
one spot, it's not Mad Max.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:30.732
- We're neck and neck with rice pudding,

00:18:30.732 --> 00:18:32.750
you've got Korean Tacos on your six.

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:34.527
- Oh my God, it's real,
we're on the Fury Road.

00:18:34.527 --> 00:18:37.820
Witness me (drowned out by music)

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.051
- Hold on tight.

00:18:39.051 --> 00:18:41.218
(screams)

00:18:50.762 --> 00:18:54.020
- Here comes the bachelor,
all dressed in my nice jacket

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.560
I only wear for special events.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:56.740
- Oh you're already on fire.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.330
- Thank you my friend, and gentlemen,

00:18:58.330 --> 00:18:59.740
welcome to my bachelor party.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.370
This is the elite party squad,

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.520
that is assuming the captain
is ready to let loose.

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:04.760
- Captain, I don't think so.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.097
I want you guys to think
of me as one of the boys,

00:19:06.097 --> 00:19:08.520
so tonight I'll be swapping
out my captains hat

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:12.490
for my Kangol hat, call me Raymond.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:13.630
- Okay Raymond in the Kangol hat,

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.580
I will definitely call you Raymond,

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:16.003
Raymond in the Kangol hat.

00:19:16.003 --> 00:19:16.836
This is the best night of my life.

00:19:16.836 --> 00:19:19.560
- Mine too, Sharon gave me
permission to get wasted.

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:21.320
She's even putting a
pasta pot next to the bed

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:22.153
in case I hurl.

00:19:22.153 --> 00:19:23.960
- Smart, I'm definitely
putting a pasta pot

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:24.860
on our wedding registry.

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.710
Charles, tell us everything
